      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-3,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/134daad8372c889b99f46b14e5894601c787aee3153f32478a776c42bc603c12.png)\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/808993ee8b53bbfc8f82324bb0699b9ca86027c626b1c144976403152b3edc03.png)\n\n- Then, translate the result by $3$ units down to get the graph of $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270407/assets/9a410de5d8168e2ae09ac91049673e1c80c3628f85cb0b32ce1dccb9cf56bc61.png)",
